 "onnxHeadersHow": "read with a hand-written protobuf field walker (scripts/onnxmeta.js), no model loaded",
 "notes": {
  "patchedCopies": "The OpenVoiceOS fp32 and int8 files do NOT load in sherpa-onnx as they are: the process exits with 'vocab_size' does not exist in the metadata (exit code -1). For measurement only, a copy of each was made with four ModelProto.metadata_props entries appended at the end of the file (vocab_size=257, normalize_type=per_feature, subsampling_factor=4, model_type=EncDecCTCModelBPE; 108 bytes, scripts/addmeta.js); graph and weights untouched. Those copies are ovos-fp32-meta and ovos-int8-meta. The fp32 copy keeps its weights in the external file model.onnx_data and loaded with the decoder process working directory set to the model folder.",
  "tokens": "OpenVoiceOS vocab.txt is identical to csndhanasekar tokens.txt apart from CRLF line endings (257 tokens).",
  "gateRssBasis": "RSS gate read on the process peak after load, warm-up and the 50 natural 5-7 s clips (max of the 4- and 2-thread runs). Over the whole 200 (clips up to 53.5 s) every model peaked between 1.1 and 1.4 GB, still under 1.5 GB.",
  "timingBasis": "Per-decode wall time = createStream + acceptWaveform + decode + getResult, audio already in memory, one warm-up decode excluded. 5-7 s set = all 50 natural 5-7 s clips of the 591-row test split (mean 6.11 s).",
  "contention": "Another session ran a Next dev server and Playwright on the same laptop during the runs. Machine CPU load just before each run is in runs[].cpuLoadBefore (1-93 %); coresBusyDuringTiming shows the decoder process itself got about 3.8-3.9 cores at 4 threads and about 1.95 at 2 threads. The 120M int8 4-thread timing was repeated on an idle CPU (1 %) and matched (p50 1,020 vs 1,015 ms).",
  "sleep": "The laptop slept during the 600M 4-thread full run (resume events 02:03 and 22:00 on 16 Nov). Its 5-7 s timing phase finished before the sleep; the largest per-clip real-time factor in the full run was 0.62 against a median 0.42, so no clip time carries the sleep.",
  "cpu": "AMD Ryzen 5 5600H is Zen 3: AVX2, no AVX-512, no AVX-VNNI. Every int8 file here is dynamic-quantised (DynamicQuantizeLinear + MatMulInteger + ConvInteger) and none failed to load on the CPU provider (no ConvInteger error), but each was slower than fp32: same export, fp32 270 ms vs int8 1,477 ms p50 at 4 threads.",
  "groqBudget": "Groq x-ratelimit-remaining-requests read 1999 after request 1 and 1800 after request 200 (daily limit 2,000). Audio-seconds remaining (rolling hourly window of 7,200) read 6,256 after request 200.",
  "notMeasured": "No Groq run with the app's own prompt; no Tanglish or code-mixed audio (FLEURS is read Tamil); no office or phone-mic audio; no run inside Next 15; no streaming. Accuracy on this laptop's microphone and on the Collector's Tanglish is unverified."
 }
}